# Package layering (AiT toolbox — aissh)

Authoritative detail: [docs/tools/aissh-internals.md#package-layering](../../docs/tools/aissh-internals.md#package-layering). Keep this rule in sync when that section changes.

## Call chain

`cmd/ssh` → `internal/ssh` (package **`aissh`**: `Run`, `Execute`, `NewManager`) → `internal/ssh/<cmd>` (closed loop per subcommand) → `internal/pkg/*` (shared, no product subcommand ownership).

**Directory vs package:** `internal/ssh/` uses Go package `aissh` (binary `aitssh`, plugin command `ssh`, `cmd/ssh`; directory is short `ssh`). Registered subcommand dirs use package names matching Cobra (`shell`, `session`, …). **`internal/ssh/connect/`** is the SSH connect route package (not registered as a Cobra subcommand).

## Subcommand package (`internal/ssh/<cmd>/`)

One package per top-level command owns: `Name`, `flags.go`, `parse.go`, `cmd.go` (`New`), `help.go`, `run.go`, **`register.go`** (`init` → `registry.Register`).

- **No** `internal/pkg/aitcmd` or names-only constant packages.
- **No** thin `internal/ssh/<cmd>/` wrappers with parse elsewhere (one closed-loop package per command).

## Registry (OCP)

- Root: `registry.AttachRoot` in `internal/ssh/cli_root.go`; root help via `registry.RootHelpEntries()` / `pkg/helpdoc.WriteRootHelp`（[`registry/root_help.go`](internal/ssh/registry/root_help.go)）。
- **Do not** hand-edit `AddCommand` lists for new top-level or nested commands.
- New top-level: `internal/ssh/<cmd>/` + `_ "…/registry/all/imports.go"`.
- Nested (`aitssh config` / `ssh config`, …): parent `<parent>/subregistry` + child `register.go` + `<parent>/registry/all/imports.go`. Ops AI admin commands live under **`internal/ait/agent`** (not under `internal/ssh`).

## Package name = command name

**Exception:** `internal/ssh/` root is package **`aissh`** (directory `ssh`, binary `aitssh`, plugin `ssh`). Otherwise directory/package = Cobra name (`shell`, `session`, `config/set`). **`internal/ssh/connect/`** is the connect route (not `registry.Register`). No `*cmd` package suffix. Agent loop kernel: **`internal/pkg/agentcore`** + **`internal/pkg/agentui`** + **`internal/pkg/agentops`** + **`internal/pkg/agentwire`**; **`internal/ait/agent`** wires admin CLI + connect; interactive Loop: **`internal/ait/loop`** via **`internal/ait/router`**. Plugin exec: **`internal/pkg/tooldispatch`**. **`internal/ait` must not import `internal/ssh`**, `internal/log`, `internal/host`, or `internal/img` (use `tooldispatch`). CLI `session`: `internal/ssh/session` (alias pkg session as `pkgsession`).

## `ait` toolbox entry (`internal/ait/`)

- **`router/`** — top-level argv routing (Loop, `agent` admin, plugin aliases, `shell` REPL).
- **`loop/`** — starts Agent Loop (`agent.RunLoop` wrapper).
- **`dispatch/`** — top-level plugin execution (`tooldispatch`).
- **`agent/`** — `ait agent` Cobra admin subtree (`connect`, `model`, `provider`, `ollama`, `config`).
- Root package **`ait`** — `Run`, `Execute`, shell REPL, help; Agent Loop via `ait` / `ait agent` (**no** standalone `cmd/ai` binary).

## `helpdoc`

- Shared: `internal/pkg/helpdoc`. Per-command: `internal/ssh/<cmd>/help.go` (nested: `<parent>/<sub>/help.go`).

## `clihints` (Try SSOT)

- Shared errhint Try example lines: [`internal/pkg/clihints`](internal/pkg/clihints/try_lines.go).
- `internal/ssh` and `internal/pkg/ssh/*` reference `clihints` constants; do not duplicate literals such as `aitssh session --list`.

## `internal/pkg`

- Shared OpenSSH argv: `internal/pkg/ssh/openssh`.
- **Must not** import `internal/ssh`.
- Meta `!ait get`/`put`: protocol names in `internal/pkg/ssh/client/transfer` (`CmdGet`/`CmdPut`); test alignment with `get.Name` / `put.Name` in `internal/ssh`.

## Refactors

Semantic unchanged; **R1–R19**, **A20–A22**; gate: `make fmt && make vet && make test && make build && make test-cross`.
